==Czech==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|cs}} {{term/t|sla-pro|*jaro}}, {{term/t|sla-pro|*jarъ}}, {{term/t|sla-pro|*jarь}}, {{term/t|sla-pro|*jara}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|cs}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*yōro-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*yeh₁ro-||year, spring}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*yeh₁r-}}. Cognate with {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|year|lang=en}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Jahr||year|lang=de}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{term/t|la|hōra||hour, time, season}}, Ancient Greek {{term|ὥρα||year, season|tr=hōra|lang=grc}}.<ref>{{R:Rejzek 2007}}</ref><ref>{{R:Machek 1968}}</ref>

